  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Indrakumar S/O Sawaldas Nagdeve vs State Of Maharashtra Thr Pso., ... on 18 November, 2025 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Nagpur Bench : Nagpur Criminal Application (Aba) No.866/2025 (Indrakumar S/o Sawaldas Nagdeve Vs. State of Maharashtra, through Police Station Offi Gadchiroli) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Office Notes, Office Memoranda of Coram, Court's or Judge's orders appearances, Court's orders of directions and Registrar's orders -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Mr. K.S. Motwani, Advocate for the applicant. Coram: Mrs.Vrushali V. Joshi, J. Dated: 18.11.2025. Heard.",
    "facts": "4. The applicant is apprehending arrest in Crime No.518/2025 for the offence punishable under Sections 123, 223, 274, 275 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita read with Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 3(1)(zz)(iv) and 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act. 5. The raid was conducted as the information was received that scented tobacco is carried out in one vehicle. Said vehicle was stopped in front of the shop of this applicant. 6. The allegations are made that the applicant is the purchaser of said scented tobacco and, therefore, the crime is registered.",
    "arguments": "7. The learned Advocate for the applicant has stated that the person who brought the tobacco to the doorstep of the shop of applicant is already taken in custody and released on bail. There is no role attributed to this applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "7. The learned Advocate for the applicant has stated that the person who brought the tobacco to the doorstep of the shop of applicant is already taken in custody and released on bail. There is no role attributed to this applicant.",
